---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Use | Jjodel"
  description="Terms of use of the Jjodel application at app.jjodel.io."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>Terms of Use</h1>
      <p class="muted">Last updated: 18 October 2026</p>

      <h2 class="mt-xl">Who provides Jjodel</h2>
      <p class="muted">
        Jjodel (app.jjodel.io) is a modeling environment for research and
        teaching, provided free of charge by the University of L'Aquila
        (Università degli Studi dell'Aquila, Italy) and developed with
        Mälardalen University and Fondazione Bruno Kessler. By creating an
        account or using the application you accept these terms.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-xl">Your account</h2>
      <p class="muted">
        You need an account to save projects on our servers. Give accurate
        information when you register and keep your password to yourself: you
        are responsible for what happens under your account. Tell us at{' '}
        <a href="mailto:info@jjodel.io">info@jjodel.io</a> if you think someone
        else has used it. You can ask us to delete your account at any time
        from the same address.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-xl">Your content</h2>
      <p class="muted">
        Metamodels, models, viewpoints, transformations and any other content
        you create remain yours. You give us only the permission we need to
        store, process and display that content in order to run the service
        for you and for the people you choose to share it with. When you share
        a project, the people you share it with can see your name, your
        nickname and the shared content.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-xl">Acceptable use</h2>
      <p class="muted">
        Use Jjodel for modeling, research and teaching. Do not upload unlawful
        content or content you have no right to share, do not try to access
        other users' data or accounts, do not interfere with the service or
        its infrastructure, and do not run automated traffic that degrades it
        for others. We may suspend accounts that break these rules.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-xl">AI features</h2>
      <p class="muted">
        The Jjodie assistant works with an API key that you provide for a
        provider of your choice (for example Anthropic, OpenAI or Google).
        When you use it, the content of your requests is sent to that
        provider and is subject to its own terms and privacy policy. We do not
        supply or pay for these keys, and AI output may be wrong: check it
        before relying on it.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-xl">Open source</h2>
      <p class="muted">
        The source code of Jjodel is released under the MIT License and is
        available on{' '}
        <a
          href="https://github.com/jjodel-modeling/jjodel-frontend"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          target="_blank"
        >
          GitHub ↗
        </a>. These terms cover the hosted service at app.jjodel.io, not your
        use of the code, which the license governs.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-xl">Availability and warranty</h2>
      <p class="muted">
        Jjodel is research software offered as is. We work to keep it
        available and your data safe, but we cannot guarantee uninterrupted
        service or the absence of errors, and features may change between
        releases. Export the projects you depend on from time to time. To the
        extent permitted by law, the University of L'Aquila is not liable for
        indirect damages or for loss of data or profit arising from the use of
        the service.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-xl">Personal data</h2>
      <p class="muted">
        How we handle the personal data of registered users is described in
        the <a href="/app-privacy/">Privacy Notice of the Jjodel application</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-xl">Changes and governing law</h2>
      <p class="muted">
        We may update these terms; the date at the top of this page shows the
        current version, and significant changes will be announced in the
        application. These terms are governed by Italian law.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-xl">Contact</h2>
      <p class="muted">
        <a href="mailto:info@jjodel.io">info@jjodel.io</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
